# Hubble CLI Troubleshooting & Flow Inspection Guide

This guide covers real-time network flow analysis and packet drop inspection using the Cilium `hubble` CLI.

## 1. Prerequisites & Status Verification

Ensure Cilium Hubble relay and port-forwarding are running on the control plane node:

```bash
# Verify Cilium Hubble is enabled in the cluster
cilium status --wait

# Start Hubble port-forward in the background if not active
cilium hubble port-forward &

# Verify local Hubble connectivity
hubble status
```

---

## 2. Tracing NetworkPolicy Drops in Real-Time

When troubleshooting NetworkPolicies, use `--verdict DROPPED` to capture packets rejected by eBPF rules:

```bash
# Watch dropped packets live across the default namespace
hubble observe --namespace default --verdict DROPPED -f

# Filter drops specifically originating from the test client pod
hubble observe --pod default/netpol-test-client --verdict DROPPED

# Filter drops targeting the httpbingo backend pod
hubble observe --pod default/httpbingo --verdict DROPPED
```

Common drop reasons captured in output:

- `Policy denied (INGRESS)`: Inbound traffic rejected by a default-deny or missing ingress rule.
- `Policy denied (EGRESS)`: Outbound request rejected by missing CoreDNS or egress whitelist rules.

---

## 3. Monitoring DNS Queries and Resolutions

To debug DNS issues when pods cannot resolve in-cluster or external hostnames:

```bash
# Observe DNS resolution flows live in default namespace
hubble observe --namespace default --protocol dns -f

# Monitor CoreDNS traffic specifically in kube-system
hubble observe --namespace kube-system --protocol dns -f
```

---

## 4. Inspecting L7 HTTP & Gateway API Traffic

Inspect HTTP request methods, paths, and status codes traversing NGINX Gateway Fabric:

```bash
# Trace HTTP requests and response codes across namespaces
hubble observe --namespace default --protocol http -f

# Trace incoming proxied flows from nginx-gateway to backend workloads
hubble observe --from-namespace nginx-gateway --to-namespace default -f

# Compact one-line flow format for high-throughput troubleshooting
hubble observe --namespace default -o compact
```
